%2C_Globe%2C_and_Anchor"]}]}      \n\nevent: delta\ndata: {"p": "/message/content/parts/0", "o": "append", "v": " and holding a \\u201cSemper Fidelis\\u201d"}      \n\ndata: {"type": "title_generation", "title": "Marine Corps Seal history", "conversation_id": "688f93a6-a128-8330-8f2c-203efebb66ed"}\n\nevent: delta\ndata: {"p": "", "o": "patch", "v": [{"p": "/message/content/parts/0", "o": "append", "v": " scroll in its beak \\ue200cite\\ue202turn3view0\\ue201"}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references", "o": "append", "v": [{"matched_text": "\\ue200cite\\ue202turn3view0\\ue201", "start_idx": 1721, "end_idx": 1738, "safe_urls": [], "refs": [], "alt": null, "prompt_text": null, "type": "hidden", "invalid": true}]}]}  \n\nevent: delta\ndata: {"v": [{"p": "/message/content/parts/0", "o": "append", "v": ". A fouled anchor in bronze sits behind the globe against a scarlet background, representing the Corps\\u2019 naval heritage \\ue200cite\\ue202turn1view0\\ue201. Surrounding the central device is a dark blue band edged in a gold rope, bearing the legend \\u201cDEPARTMENT OF THE NAVY \\u2022 UNITED STATES MARINE CORPS\\u201d in gold letters \\ue200cite\\ue202turn1view0\\ue201.\\n\\n## Usage Restrictions  \\nUnder 32 CFR 765.14(c)(1), reproduction and use of the Marine Corps seal are restricted to materials eman"}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references/9/safe_urls", "o": "append", "v": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle%2C_Globe%2C_and_Anchor"]}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references/9/alt", "o": "replace", "v": "([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle%2C_Globe%2C_and_Anchor))"}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references/9/type", "o": "replace", "v": "grouped_webpages"}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references/9/invalid", "o": "remove"}, {"p": "/message/metadata/content_references/9", "o": "append", "v": {"items": [{"title": "Eagle, Globe, and Anchor - Wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle%2C_Globe%2C_and_Anchor", "pub_da